# 67 berry harvest, minted on 66's end save (the Cheri Berry planted and watered in berry tree 9, the player below it
# on Route 104): only the game clock moves on, 13 hours, as the cartridge's RTC running that long would. The GBA RTC
# does not take a recipe `clock` (PC_RTC): every run starts it at 2004-01-01 10:00:00 (games/gba-common/pc/src/
# gba_rtc.c), so the clock moves through the game's own RTC offset, SaveBlock2's localTimeOffset (local time = RTC -
# offset, src/rtc.c:293-324); lastBerryTreeUpdate and the tree are left as 66's play wrote them.
# Growth: DoTimeBasedEvents on CONTINUE's map load (src/overworld.c:618,1477 -> src/clock.c:27-74) passes the minutes
# since lastBerryTreeUpdate (66: the RTC's 10:00:17) to BerryTreeTimeUpdate (src/berry.c:1239-1287). Cheri's stage is
# 3 h (src/berry.c:292, 1413-1416: 180 min): PLANTED -> SPROUTED -> TALLER -> FLOWERING -> BERRIES after
# 4 x 180 = 720 min, and the berries stay for 4 x 180 more (src/berry.c:1281-1282), so ~780 min lands in BERRIES
# (< 71 x 180, the unwatered reset, src/berry.c:1254-1257).
clock-advance 780
